+++ b/docs/loom/intent/2026-09-02-scripts-share-git-helper.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Scripts share git helper
+originator: kouko
+kind: engineering
+needs-design: no — internal refactor, no surface the user reads or types into
+evidence: [scripts/archive.py, scripts/clean.py, scripts/fetch.py, scripts/report.py, scripts/sync.py, scripts/tag.py, tests/test_smoke.py]
+status: open
+
+## Problem
+Six scripts each carry the same Git command-running behavior, so every correction or improvement must be repeated six times and can drift.
+
+## Proposed outcome
+Move that behavior into one shared helper and make all six scripts use it without changing what their users observe.
+
+## Acceptance
+1. The Git command-running behavior has one implementation used by all six scripts.
+2. Every script still prints the current branch name when its command succeeds.
+3. Every script still reports a failed Git command as a runtime error containing Git's error message.
+
+## Constraints
+- Preserve the six scripts' observable behavior.
+- Add no third-party dependency.
+
+## Out of scope
+- Changing command-line arguments, output formatting, or the Git command each script runs.
+
+## Open questions
+- none

